  "consts": [
   "core/osr_learn.py - turn historical OSR exports into per-layout consensus.\n\nV2.0.19.12: close the learning loop. The OSR (``OSR-Sales Order Summary\nReport.xlsx``) is a write-only sink today; this module reads it BACK and derives,\nfor each template, the stable header fields that were CONSISTENTLY the same\nacross past POs (country of origin, currency, price term, product group, ...).\nThose consensus values are then used at extraction time to FILL BLANKS (never\noverwrite a parsed value) on POs of the same layout - zero AI - which also\nreplaces the self-heal AI loop for stable fields.\n\nDesign\n------\n- The consensus store is ``%APPDATA%/Purchase Order Extractor V2/osr_learning.json``\n  (kept SEPARATE from the recipe cache so it never pollutes a ``PoRecipe`` and\n  never triggers the overwrite semantics of ``apply_field_defaults``).\n- Grouping key: ``fp::<fingerprint>`` when the OSR carries the ``_Fingerprint``\n  meta column (V2.0.19.12+ exports), else ``sig::<customer>`` as a best-effort\n  fallback for already-saved 31-column files (in practice one customer == one\n  template; the LPP family shares one fingerprint AND one customer).\n- A field is learned only when its value agrees across >= ``agreement`` fraction\n  of that group's rows (default 0.9), so an occasional wrong/stray value is never\n  propagated across POs.\n",
